"id":"min_completion_time",
"source":"min_completion_time.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    data = raw.split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n\n    n = int(data[0])\n    times = []\n    for k in range(n):\n        t = int(data[1 + k])\n        times.append(t)\n\n    order = sorted(times)\n\n    total = 0\n    finish = 0\n    for t in order:\n        finish += t\n        total += finish\n\n    print(*order)\n    print(total)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program sorts the job times ascending, then walks the sorted list keeping a running finish time and adding each job's finish time to a total, which is the sum of every finish time.",
